  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>-subshell&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Orbital angular momentum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>mvr</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> orbital, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> (azimuthal quantum number) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> orbital angular momentum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mn>0</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mn>0</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;the orbital angular momentum of an electron in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> -orbital is&nbsp;Zero.</p>",
